   P=s**2/40 - s/2 + 3      T=1.30  quad=+0.0000049396  exact=+0.0000049396  |d|=2.9e-17
====================================================================================
2. Sign test must ACCEPT an even-multiplicity zero at the contact radius
====================================================================================
   -(s - 4)**2                  (double zero at s=4) -> True : ok: sign on (a,inf) = -1, multiplicity at a = 2
   4 - s                        (simple zero at s=4) -> True : ok: sign on (a,inf) = -1, multiplicity at a = 1
   -(s - 6)*(s - 4)**2          (double at 4, simple at 6) -> False : odd-multiplicity root(s) in (4,inf): [(6, 1)] (sign flips => not -1)
   -1                           (constant -1) -> True : ok: sign on (a,inf) = -1, multiplicity at a = 0
   (v-1)^2                      (double zero at v=1) -> True : ok: sign on (a,inf) = 1, multiplicity at a = 0
   v-1                          (simple zero at v=1) -> False : odd-multiplicity root(s) in (0,inf): [(1, 1)] (sign flips => not 1)
====================================================================================
3. Candidate certification (Kepler comparison reduced to rationals + pi)
====================================================================================
   P = -(s - 4)**2              -> f(0)=-16, f^(0)~-31/4 : need both positive
   P = -(s - 8)/4               -> sign failure: CE1 odd-multiplicity root(s) in (4,inf): [(8, 1)] (sign flips => not -1) / CE2 ok
   P = -(s - 4)*(s + 10)/10     -> sign failure: CE1 ok / CE2 odd-multiplicity root(s) in (0,inf): [(11/2 + sqrt(230)/2, 1)] (sign flips => not 1)

====================================================================================
4. Directed pi enclosure and the exact Kepler test
====================================================================================
   pi in [3.14159265358979311600, 3.14159265358979311600]  (width 6.67e-68)
   acceptance threshold: bound < pi/sqrt18  <=>  P0/Q0 < sqrt(pi^3/32) = 0.98435062
      P0/Q0 = 99/100     32 P0^2 = 313632       vs pi^3 Q0^2 = 310062.766803 => kepler_ok = False
      P0/Q0 = 1          32 P0^2 = 32           vs pi^3 Q0^2 = 31.006277    => kepler_ok = False
      P0/Q0 = 2/3        32 P0^2 = 128          vs pi^3 Q0^2 = 279.056490   => kepler_ok = True
      P0/Q0 = 49/50      32 P0^2 = 307328       vs pi^3 Q0^2 = 310062.766803 => kepler_ok = True
      P0/Q0 = 9843/10000  32 P0^2 = 3100308768   vs pi^3 Q0^2 = 3100627668.029982 => kepler_ok = True
      P0/Q0 = 2461/2500  32 P0^2 = 3100938752   vs pi^3 Q0^2 = 3100627668.029982 => kepler_ok = False
   A successful certificate reports P(0)/Q(0) rational and the test
        32 P(0)^2 < pi^3 Q(0)^2  (<=> bound (4/(3 sqrt pi))P0/Q0 < pi/sqrt18),
   decided with rational enclosures of pi; the SEARCH over P is a separate LP.
   No float residual is used as an identity: the map is applied by exact
   differentiation, and only the quadrature cross-check above is floating point.
